{"name":"Wing Commander","hex":"#0065ac","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Wing Commander","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of wing commander ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wing_Commander"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wing commander","blocks":[{"text":"Wing commander is a senior officer rank used by some air forces, with origins from the Royal Air Force. The rank is used by air forces of many countries that have historical British influence."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing_commander"},{"title":"Wing Commander (franchise)","blocks":[{"text":"Wing Commander is a media franchise consisting of space combat simulation video games from Origin Systems, Inc., an animated television series, a feature film, a collectible card game, a series of novels, and action figures. The franchise originated in 1990 with the release of the video game Wing Commander."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing_Commander_(franchise)"},{"title":"Wing","blocks":[{"text":"A wing is a structure which produces both lift and drag while moving through air. Wings are defined by two shape characteristics, an airfoil section and a planform. Wing efficiency is expressed as lift-to-drag ratio, which compares the benefit of lift with the air resistance of a given wing shape, as it flies. Aerodynamics includes the study of wing performance in air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg/330px-Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing"},{"title":"Commander","blocks":[{"text":"Commander is a common naval officer rank as well as a job title in many armies. Commander is also used as a level 8 rank or title in other formal organizations, including several police forces. In several countries, this naval rank is termed as a frigate captain."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commander"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/RNAS_Wg_Cdr.png/120px-RNAS_Wg_Cdr.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/RNAS_Wg_Cdr.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/RNAS_Wg_Cdr.png/120px-RNAS_Wg_Cdr.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The rank insignia of a Royal Naval Air Service wing commander","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARNAS_Wg_Cdr.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/RAF-Wg_Cdr-OF-4.png/120px-RAF-Wg_Cdr-OF-4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/RAF-Wg_Cdr-OF-4.png/250px-RAF-Wg_Cdr-OF-4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/RAF-Wg_Cdr-OF-4.png/120px-RAF-Wg_Cdr-OF-4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARAF-Wg_Cdr-OF-4.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/TaT-Air_Guard-OF-4.png/120px-TaT-Air_Guard-OF-4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/TaT-Air_Guard-OF-4.png/250px-TaT-Air_Guard-OF-4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/TaT-Air_Guard-OF-4.png/120px-TaT-Air_Guard-OF-4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaT-Air_Guard-OF-4.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f